! mcp_bootstrap_p215.strap -- MCP printed page 215: the V-section branch
! table (V DISP, V OFFON, V BYP) and V BSTRT .. V REE1.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.222, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
!  CARD ID CA000085  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 215"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224147, line 1's word.
!
! Finding aid: tools/page_sheet.py 215.  Every value below is read off
! the IMAGE.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, contiguous from 224147.00 to 224200.40.
!   p.214's sheet ends at 224146.40 (a half word); p.216's begins at
!   224201.00.  Both joins are contiguous (neither page landed yet).
!   line 37  V CSAW SYN(BU,1),V RDCSS.19 prints 224171.23+ +00000000
!            BU,01 ,10: a !SYM, no !CHECK.
!   line 48  no statement and no location: only the remark "-019" and
!            serial 0A000128.  Compiles nothing; not transcribed.
!
! >>> REMARKS ARE NUMBERS. <<<  The comment column prints "-0122" ..
! "-0167" (line 11 prints none) at one indent, and "-020", "-021",
! "-019" (lines 31, 46, 48) and "-0122", "-0147", "-0153", "-0159"
! (lines 2, 26, 33, 40) further left.  Recorded on each card as printed.
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  The header prints CARD ID "CA000085" (open
! first glyph); the right-hand column prints "0A000085" .. "0A000130"
! with a closed round first glyph.  Recorded, not resolved.  Shared
! serials: lines 1/2 (085), 25/26 (108), 32/33 (114), 39/40 (120);
! otherwise one per line, no gaps, line 48's blank card included (128).
! Asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 3, 26 and 46.
!
! >>> O PRINTED AS AN OPEN C, AND THE NAMES SPELLED WITH O. <<<
! Line 4's label prints "V CFFON" and its statement "V CNLIN"; line 5
! "V CFFLN".  At 900 dpi the first glyph of each is an open round, while
! the O of OFFLB/ONLIB (lines 12-13) and the 4th glyph of CFFON itself
! print closed.  The symbols are the ON-LINE/OFF-LINE pair of the
! ONLIB/OFFLB on lines 12-13, and this drum opens round glyphs
! (transcription_workflow.md "O vs C"; octal fields on this page print
! 0 open throughout, e.g. "C0C000.23").  Spelled VOFFON, VONLIN,
! VOFFLN.  NOT assembly-checked: VONLIN/VOFFLN are external and their
! values come from this page's binary, and nothing here references
! VOFFON -- the integrating merge must confirm the spelling.
!
! >>> "V NCP" IS VNOP (assembly-bound). <<<  Line 18's label and line
! 43's second operand print "V NCP"; lines 17 and 19 print "V NOP".
! Line 17's B,V NOP prints 224157.50 = line 18's 224157.40 + B's .10,
! and line 43's h2 224157.74 is that same address; so one symbol.
!
! >>> "V L" ON LINE 34 IS V U. <<<  Its U is worn to an L (right
! stroke short), as is the U of "V SU" on line 41; its binary
! 225232.07 01 is identical to lines 21/46 LVI,V U,V CR.
!
! >>> "V RDEE" ON LINE 24. <<<  The fourth letter is a worn E (faint
! arms) -- read as RDEL at 400 dpi.  Sibling labels REE1/3/4/7, EE,
! EE1.  Nothing on this page references it: ink only.
!
! >>> LINE 28'S BYTE PRINTS "C5" AND IS 05. <<<  Same open round as
! line 47's "C1" two lines down (which assembles to 01, as lines 21/34
! print it) and as this row's octal "C0C000"; line 22 V+I,,1. prints 05.
!
! Line 45 prints CM0C00 (4th glyph open); a connective is four binary
! digits, so CM0000, and the printed h2 001000.00 F0 agrees.
!
! LINE 44 prints "BZBZ,V CSAW," -- a null branch field, written as
! printed: a null field compiles as zero (C22-6531 printed p.7; C28-6129 PDF pp.8-9).
! The printed h2 000000.34 04 is address zero.
!
! EXTERNAL SYMBOLS.  No V symbol is landed.  Every V value below is
! from THIS PAGE's binary.  Index numbers from the I field: B's low
! byte (VU 03), LVI/SVA/V+I's 2J+1 in the low octal pair (VT1 .11=4,
! VT2 .15=6, VT5 .23=9, VU .07=3).

